; form-cli-landing-band.bml — the landing door reads its witness's exit, and a red witness holds the landing; its git
; steps are argv children whose exits the host answers.
; Verdict 262143
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY (host_spawn_at and host_wait run each child; no sibling kernel carries them)
;
; Each claim asks the readers and steps of form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-landing.bml, never ld-land itself: no claim adds,
; commits or pushes in this checkout (git runs only over scratch repositories under temp_dir). The witnesses are tiny
; shell commands spawned by the landing's own carrier (ld-witness-at), with their evidence under temp_dir.
;     1  a witness that exits 0 reads exit 0, and it holds nothing
;     2  a witness that exits 3 reads exit 3, and it holds the landing
;     4  a witness that prints the mark itself and then exits 5 reads 5: the exit is the host's, never a printed line
;     8  no witness named holds nothing
;    16  a launch host_spawn_at refused at birth has no exit, and holds the landing
;    32  with everything else ready, a red witness is the reason held, and the [landing] line names its exit
;    64  of a present tracked file and a path that is neither present nor tracked, only the present one is
;        addable, and the other is named unstaged: one unmatched pathspec would make git add stage nothing
;   128  a path that is neither present nor tracked reads untracked (git ls-files answers it nothing)
;   256  in a scratch repository under temp_dir, two tracked files removed from the tree (one named café.txt,
;        which git's own listing would quote) read tracked in the spelling they were named, an untracked absent
;        path does not, and git add of the two stages both removals
;   512  forty paths stage through --pathspec-from-file in a scratch repository: past the 32 words an argv holds
;  1024  forty tracked files removed from the tree read tracked, chunked under the argv cap; a path git tracks as a
;        directory reads tracked; a path with glob characters is a literal one
;  2048  in a scratch origin: the commit, the push and the push of main each say their own exit, a push main
;        refused reads behind, a restart puts the branch on origin/main, and a restart whose fetch fails stops there
;  4096  the census counts what a child costs: host_wait, host_capture and host_spawn_quiet are registered as
;        local-process rows with tags no other row holds, and a child reaped inside a window moves that plane
;  8192  a path is literal, never a glob: in a scratch repository holding f2.txt and a file named f[0-9]*.txt, adding
;        the path "f[0-9]*.txt" stages that one file and not f2.txt (git add without --literal-pathspecs stages both)
; 16384  the reunion after a push behind origin (form-cli-reunion.bml, argv by directory), in a scratch origin: a landing
;        commit that conflicts with main on the drawn page and on a river is joined (the river by union, each row once in
;        order; the page remade through the redraw door, a stub argv here, into the landing's own commit) and pushed
;        ("[push] exit=0 after the reunion", one commit ahead of main); a landing that conflicts on mod.bml, a file the
;        body does not know, keeps both banks under .form-heal/reunion-unlearned, aborts the rebase, stands where it stood
;        and reads "the rows did not join"; the keep path is absolute, and the redraw runs in the checkout (its stub's
;        paths are relative)
; 32768  a rebase git refuses with nothing unmerged (an unstaged change in the checkout) says what git said ("the rebase
;        was refused: ... unstaged ..."), keeps no banks, leaves the branch where it stood and reads "did not join"
; 65536  the side taken for a conflicting page is main's: with a redraw that changes nothing (`true`), the page that
;        stands after the reunion is main's bytes, never the landing's
;131072  the default wiring (fcr-reunion(): the checkout "." and the argv ./fkwu observe/rent-ladder-page-run.bml) in a
;        scratch checkout: a child kernel run in that directory (env -C) drives it with a stub `fkwu` script there that
;        records its argv; the stub reads "./fkwu observe/rent-ladder-page-run.bml", the page it drew stands in the
;        landing's commit, one ahead of main, pushed. The scratch checkout links this checkout's form/ and runtime/ (a
;        kernel lowers from the directory it runs in; the process cannot change its own), and its `fkwu` is the stub.
